    "title": "Even-intersecting families of lattice paths and the Catalan numbers",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23608134",
    "publication_date": "2026-10-24",
    "description": "<p>We classify every family of 2^n North-East lattice paths from (0,0) to (n,n) with even pairwise numbers of common edges: each is determined by a unique noncrossing perfect matching of the step positions. There are exactly C_n extremal families. More generally, all equality cases of the binary-word inequality are classified by noncrossing partial matchings with no unmatched point under an arc. The complete written proof applies to every length and reproves the underlying inequality; it is independent of finite computation. This revision adds an explicit coordinate range for the cell lemma, three vector diagrams, a proof audit and independent geometric-edge verification. Fresh SAT checks and seven bounded core-Lean kernel checks accompany it. The all-length theorem is not formalized. Prepared for possible Annals of Mathematics submission; no journal submission or acceptance is claimed. Original preprint: https://hexagonmath.org/2610.00474v1 . Source and verification files: https://github.com/creelie/Paper_3 .</p>",
